    {"text":"CLOSEST DRIVE TEST","size":"large","align":"center"},
    {"text":"Park the helicopter on flat ground with 120 m of free space around it and stay still. TEST 1: is a closest point in a drive chosen when the drive starts or when the crew reaches it? One drive (far point, then closest) against two drives. TEST 2: a route that is a single point at 0 to 10 m from the crew, at 1, 2 and 5 m/s: does it return, how long, how far does the crew go? TEST 3: the second hoist_crew drive of the hospital handover (closest of four points 2 m around a stretcher, the crew 1.5 m from it). TEST 4: a closest with the crew standing on the candidate point (0 m) or 0.3 m from it, the case of the quad SAR. TEST 5: test 3 with a second crew object standing on the point the crew drives to. Each line shows if the drive returned, the time, the farthest distance from the start and where the crew ends. A drive that does not return in 30 s (60 s for test 1) is reported NOT DONE and the object is removed."},
